  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $62.5B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security recorded 26,832 awards with an average award size of $2.3M, and obligations are up 120.7% year over year. The current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligations at $28.7B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $7.8B and Security Guards and Patrol Services at $4B. FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO is the largest vendor with $13.4B in obligations, followed by BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED at $4.5B and DAVIE DEFENSE INC. at $3.5B. The FY21 through FY26 series shows a step change with FY21 at $19.7B, FY22 at $20.8B, FY23 at $23.9B, FY24 at $23.6B, FY25 at $28.3B, and FY26 at $62.5B. Use this summary to focus acquisition strategy, capture plans, and subcontracting targets within the largest NAICS and vendor pockets of spending.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has DHS contract spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $62.5B in FY26 to date, up 120.7% year over year. Fiscal comparisons show steady growth from FY21 at $19.7B to FY25 at $28.3B before the FY26 to date total of $62.5B. The Department of Homeland Security is issuing 26,832 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $2.3M. The current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date, which affects direct annual comparisons."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the biggest product and vendor opportunities at DHS?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction leads obligations at $28.7B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $7.8B and Security Guards and Patrol Services at $4B. FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO holds the largest vendor share with $13.4B, then BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED at $4.5B and DAVIE DEFENSE INC. at $3.5B. Computer Systems Design Services and Other Computer Related Services together account for $2.1B and $1.9B respectively, indicating sustained demand for IT services. Engineering Services and travel-related services also appear among top categories with $1.4B and $1.2B."
      }
    ]
  },
